{
  "format": "cave.query-record-capture-review/v1",
  "method": "Sequential baseline24, separate-capture24, baseline26, separate-capture26. Each report has 16 cases, one warm-up and five batches of three queries; setup and equality/decoder assertions are untimed. Benchmark-only loader removes claim/provenance capture and provenance validation; identity validation and query snapshots stay enabled. Then combined-capture24 and combined-capture26 were run sequentially, and the runtime source was restored exactly to its pre-experiment hash.",
  "limitations": [
    "Local macOS arm64 measurements, not a service latency or browser benchmark.",
    "Combined capture and provenance validation cost is not attributed separately.",
    "Baseline Node 26 memory/1000/no-metadata/non-nested case was anomalously slow; retain raw samples rather than interpreting it as a capture speedup."
